# EdgeLens — Cursor IDE rules
#
# Drop this file at the project root as `.cursorrules`. Cursor will
# load it as instructions for every completion in the workspace.

You write tests against the EdgeLens Edge AI Device Farm — a service
that hands out real edge-AI cameras (Seeed reCamera, RISC-V + Sophgo
NPU) over the network. EdgeLens is framework-native — use the test
runner the project already uses (pytest, Playwright, k6, Robot); do
not invent an EdgeLens-specific runner.

# SDK surface

Python:
    from edgelens import EdgeLensClient
    client = EdgeLensClient()  # reads $EDGELENS_API_KEY

    with client.create_session(device_type="recamera-2002", os="stock-os") as session:
        session.wait_ready()
        device = session.device
        device.deploy(model="./face.cvimodel")
        stats = device.inference.run(duration=30)
        assert stats.fps.avg >= 15
        assert stats.latency_ms.p95 < 100

Async: `from edgelens.aio import AsyncEdgeLensClient` mirrors the sync
shape and is the right choice in pytest-asyncio / Node-driven tests.

pytest (with `edgelens-pytest` installed): the `device` fixture handles
allocate + wait_ready + release. Prefer it.

    def test_face_latency(device):
        device.deploy(model="./models/face.cvimodel")
        stats = device.inference.run(duration=30)
        assert stats.fps.avg >= 15

# OS tiers

- `"stock-os"` — reCamera firmware. Has `device.inference.*`, `device.display.*`, web UI, camera stream. Use when EdgeLens runs inference for you.
- `"recamagined"` — SSH-only raw OS. No built-in inference / display HTTP. Use when you ship your own binary via `device.deploy(model=..., files=[...])` + `device.exec()`. Deployed files land in `/userdata/Models/` and aren't executable; `chmod +x` first.

The SDK enum `OSType.STOCK` has value `"stock-os"` — never write
`"stock"`, that string has never worked against a live API.

# Patterns to use

- Always wrap session creation in a `with` block — release is on-exit.
- `session.wait_ready()` before touching `session.device`.
- Catch only `edgelens.errors.*` (EdgeLensError, SessionError, AuthenticationError, DeviceError, TimeoutError) — never bare `Exception`.
- One assertion per acceptance criterion; don't bundle.
- To use a different API base URL, pass `base_url=` to the client.

# Anti-patterns — do not generate

- `os="stock"` (defunct; use `"stock-os"`)
- `time.sleep(N)` to poll for ready (use `session.wait_ready()`)
- Hard-coded device hosts (`10.0.1.42`); always go through `session.device`
- Manual `session.release()` inside a `with` block (the CM does it)
- Mocking `EdgeLensClient` or `Device` in tests meant to hit real hardware — that defeats the point of EdgeLens. Mock at the model boundary instead.
- Catching `EdgeLensError` to "make the test pass" — surface the failure.

# When the user asks for a test

Identify (1) framework, (2) OS tier, (3) the actual acceptance
criterion ("fps >= 15 on the crowd_scene clip", not "make sure
inference works"). Write the thinnest test that checks the criterion.
Don't stack deploy + display + inference in one test unless that
combination is what's being checked.

# When the user hits an error

- `AuthenticationError` → `$EDGELENS_API_KEY` unset / malformed / revoked.
- `SessionError` on `wait_ready` → device flash failed; `session.error` carries the reason.
- `TimeoutError` on `wait_ready` → flash > 300s default; bump via `wait_ready(timeout=600)`.
- HTTP 429 on create → `max_concurrent_sessions` full; release prior or upgrade plan.
- HTTP 410 on `device.*` → session already released; start fresh.
- HTTP 400 with `private` in detail → SSRF block; URL DNS-resolves to a private IP. Use a public URL.
- HTTP 422 with `extra fields not permitted` → unknown key in request body. Drop it.

Always preserve the full error chain. Do not `try/except: pass`.
